  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.cleared_at IS 'When an optional receipt stopped asking for attention. Distinct from seen_at, which only means read. NULL on every obligation (CHECK).'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.clear_reason IS 'Why an optional receipt was cleared: explicit | request_open | sweep | legacy_seen. legacy_seen is reserved for the U18 cutover backfill and carries no operation id.'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.cleared_by_operation_id IS 'The clear operation that cleared this receipt. Every clear the server performs is operation-backed, whatever the reason: the operation row is what makes a replayed operationId idempotent and U09 undo possible. NULL only for the U18 legacy_seen backfill, which has no operation.'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.logical_task_key IS 'Obligation identity across renewals; one live obligation per (account_id, logical_task_key). Not a rename of attention_thread_key, which keeps its legacy meaning. Populated from U05 onwards.'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.lifecycle_generation IS 'Monotonic generation of the logical task; a renewal supersedes its predecessor, a delivery retry does not. Populated from U05 onwards.'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.notification_outbox.placement IS 'U11/D16 placement policy, not an attention class. ''primary'' takes part in dots, counts and ordering; ''timeline_only'' is visible and recoverable but excluded from every primary-surface indicator, so child activity never lights an ancestor Request.'

''',

  r'''
COMMENT ON CONSTRAINT notification_outbox__obligation_beacon_chk ON public.notification_outbox IS 'U15R-e: a live obligation belongs to a Request. Mirrors the producer rule AttentionPolicy.logicalTaskKey already enforces (it throws "Live obligation requires a Request"). Without it a requires_action row on a profile-policy destination stored with beacon_id IS NULL, was labelled surface=activity by visibleWithSurface, and had no indicator in request-attention.md §6 — which is why my desk.count could not be scoped to the myWork surface.'

''',

